---
/**
 * /wallpapers/healing — SEO landing page for the Healing / rebuild category.
 * Chrome page (ChromeLayout), fully indexable, links through to the real
 * photos at /gallery#rebuild (world key `rebuild`).
 */
import ChromeLayout from '../../layouts/ChromeLayout.astro';
---

<ChromeLayout
  title="Healing & Recovery Motivational Wallpapers | motivationalwallpaper.com"
  description="Gentle strength wallpapers for rebuilding after a hard season, one day at a time"
>
  <h1>Healing & Recovery Motivational Wallpapers</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    A quiet reminder, for whatever you're rebuilding from.
  </p>

  <p>
    Healing rarely looks dramatic from the outside — it's mostly just
    getting through an ordinary day while carrying something heavy, and
    doing it again the next day. These healing wallpapers are built for
    that kind of quiet strength: sage and clay tones with a soft, italic
    line that simply says you are still here. No pressure to have it
    figured out, no timeline attached — just an acknowledgment, waiting on
    your lock screen, that showing up today counts.
  </p>
  <p>
    This category is for anyone rebuilding after loss, a breakup, burnout,
    illness, or a season that knocked them down harder than they expected.
    It's not about forcing positivity onto a hard moment — it's a gentle,
    repeated cue that recovery is happening even on the days it doesn't feel
    like it, and that being carried through something doesn't make you any
    less strong. A small reminder, seen every time you check your phone,
    that you're still standing and that's enough for today.
  </p>

  <p class="cta">
    <a href="/gallery#rebuild">Browse the Healing wallpapers &rarr;</a>
  </p>
</ChromeLayout>

<style>
  h1 {
    font-size: var(--t-title1-size);
    font-weight: var(--t-title1-weight);
    letter-spacing: var(--t-title1-track);
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
  }
  .lead {
    font-size: var(--t-lead-size);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
  }
  p {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .cta {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }
  .cta a {
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
